{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"bald-diagnostic-cricket","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOn 2026-11-04, `make verify` on macOS (load average 24-28) failed 2 default-tier tests whose asserted stderr starts with a `--- Logging error ---` traceback (`ValueError: I/O operation on closed file`):\n\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py::test_cli_passed_but_unsigned_is_exit_11_with_byte_identical_stderr`\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py::test_cli_llm_error_is_clean_exit_one`\n\nThe failing log record is the `rebar._commands._seam._apply_authorship` warning `authorship: signing SKIPPED for event %s on %s — %s; writing unsigned` (`no resolvable identity (author_id) for this writer`), emitted from `create_ticket` while the test seeds its ticket. A logging handler still holds a stream from an earlier test's `capsys` capture, which is closed by then.\n\nDeterministic reproduction, on `origin/main` `fe6c2100292` and `1cb7ea41f0c` with no local changes: running the 2 tests together in one process, the plan-review test passes, then the verify-completion test fails, 3 of 3 runs. Running the verify-completion test alone passes. In the full `make verify` run, the plan-review test itself also failed, so some earlier test leaves the same state behind.\n\nDiscovered while verifying subsolar-sonorous-puppy, whose change touches only the importer and its test.\n\n## Next check\n\nFind which handler holds the closed stream: after the plan-review test's `rebar._cli.main([...])` call, list `logging.getLogger().handlers` and the `rebar` logger's handlers and their `stream` attributes. That tests whether the CLI entry point installs a stream handler bound to the `sys.stderr` that `capsys` had in place, and does not remove it on return.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The handler that outlives the test is identified, with the code that installs it.\n- [ ] The 2 tests above pass when run together in one process, in either order, and in the full default tier.\n- [ ] A regression test fails before the fix and passes after it.","id":"cded-334b-a742-4082","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"CLI facade tests fail on a logging handler bound to an earlier test's closed stderr"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793804207360410001,"uuid":"b7d6bca1-5a02-4b44-9c97-32b71cd0ec41"}